\pard\tx3600\tx3980\tx4340\fs28\li1500\fc0\cf0 Performs a file operation on a set of files in a particular directory. 
\i operation
\i0  is some file operation, such as compressing or moving files. 
\i files
\i0  contains NSString specifying the names of the files to be manipulated. The file names are given relative to the 
\i source
\i0  directory. The list can contain both files and directories; all of them must be located directly within source (not in one of its subdirectories). \

\fs14 \

\fs28 Some operationsÐsuch as moving, copying, and linking filesÐrequire a destination directory to be specified. If not, 
\i destination
\i0  should be the empty string (@"").\

\fs14 \

\fs28 The possible values for 
