\i0  are:\

\fs14 \

\pard\tx5740\tx6480\tx7240\tx9540\tx10280\tx11020\f2\b\fs28\li1900\fc0\cf0 Operation			Meaning\

\fs6 \

\f0\b0\fs28 NSWorkspaceMoveOperation			Move file to destination\

\fs14 \

\fs28 NSWorkspaceCopyOperation			Copy file to destination\

\fs14 \

\fs28 NSWorkspaceLinkOperation			Create link to file in destination\

\fs14 \

\fs28 NSWorkspaceCompressOperation		Compress file\

\fs14 \

\fs28 NSWorkspaceDecompressOperation		Decompress file\

\fs14 \

\fs28 NSWorkspaceEncryptOperation			Encrypt file\

\fs14 \

\fs28 NSWorkspaceDecryptOperation			Decrypt file\

\fs14 \

\fs28 NSWorkspaceDestroyOperation			Destroy file\

\fs14 \

\fs28 NSWorkspaceRecycleOperation			Move file to recycler\

\fs14 \

\fs28 NSWorkspaceDuplicateOperation		Duplicate file in source directory\

\fs14 \

\pard\tx2300\f2\b\fs24\fi-800\li2300\fc0\cf0 Note:	
\f0\b0\fs28 NSWorkspaceCompressOperation, NSWorkspaceDecompressOperation, NSWorkspaceEncryptOperation, and NSWorkspaceDecryptOperation are not available on the Microsoft Windows platform.\

\fs14 \

\pard\tx3600\tx3980\tx4340\fs28\li1500\fc0\cf0 This method returns YES if the operation succeeded, NO otherwise, In 
\i tag
\i0 , the method returns a negative integer if the operation fails, 0 if the operation is performed synchronously and succeeds, and a positive integer if the operation is performed asynchronously. The positive integer is a tag that identifies the requested file operation. Before this method returns, it posts an NSWorkspaceDidPerformFileOperationNotification to NSWorkspace's notification center.\

